  "notes": "The Torhalle has three continuous open passages, patterned red sandstone panels, slim pilasters, slate roofs, two side stair turrets and an open bell turret. The surviving three bays of the church include the buttressed west gable, Gothic window and shallow aisle arches. The two surviving buildings follow their PMTiles footprints. Façade and roof profiles are estimated from the exterior photographs and passage detail. The model includes the three open Torhalle passages and the church exterior. Medieval buildings known through archaeology remain outside the standing architectural model.",
